			<!-- Confirmed against the target laptop on 2026-08-06:
			       01:00.0 3D controller [0302]
			       NVIDIA GA107M [GeForce RTX 3050 Mobile] [10de:25a2] rev a1

			     IOPCIMatch encodes (device << 16) | vendor, so 10de:25a2
			     becomes 0x25a210de. This is now an exact match rather than
			     the vendor-wide wildcard it started as. That wildcard would
			     have claimed any NVIDIA card, which matters if this kext ever
			     loads on a machine other than the target laptop.

			     probe() still rejects non-display functions as a second
			     filter; see NV3050Probe.cpp. Note the class here is 0x0302
			     (3D controller), NOT 0x0300 (VGA controller). That is the
			     muxless signature, and probe() checks base class 0x03 only,
			     so it accepts both.

			     Do not write a double hyphen anywhere in this comment. XML
			     forbids it inside comments, and plutil/plistlib reject the
			     whole file with a parse error that does not name the line. -->
			<key>IOPCIMatch</key>
			<string>0x25a210de</string>
			<!-- Outbid IOPCIFamily's generic driver, which would otherwise
			     claim the device before we get a chance. -->
